# NOT INSTALLED BY install.sh -- kept for the case where you route
# records to a file yourself.
#
# On macOS nothing writes /var/log/cmdscribe.log: logger(1) goes to the
# unified log. Installing a rotation rule for a file that never appears is
# how a box ends up looking like it keeps logs when it keeps none.
#
# If you do add an asl rule (/etc/asl.conf) sending local0 to a file,
# install this alongside it:
#   install -m 0644 -o root -g wheel this /etc/newsyslog.d/cmdscribe.conf
#
# <logname>               <owner:group> <mode> <count> <size> <flags>
/var/log/cmdscribe.log    root:wheel    0600   12      10240 Z
